1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:04,018
What if appreciating batik could become creating something of your own?

2
00:00:04,138 --> 00:00:09,580
Wear Your Batik turns Malaysian batik inspiration into a personal, playful design experience.

3
00:00:10,350 --> 00:00:12,959
Start with an original botanical motif.

4
00:00:13,079 --> 00:00:15,198
Choose your colours and adjust the repeat.

5
00:00:15,318 --> 00:00:18,859
Every choice updates the cloth and garment preview immediately.

6
00:00:18,979 --> 00:00:24,980
You don't need design experience to begin: the guided flow helps you make something that feels like you.

7
00:00:30,350 --> 00:00:33,938
Go further with your own drawn marks or botanical stamps.

8
00:00:34,058 --> 00:00:38,144
Explore an all-over pattern, a hem border, or side panels.

9
00:00:38,264 --> 00:00:42,206
These are contemporary digital interpretations inspired by batik.

10
00:00:45,350 --> 00:00:48,235
Now explore your design in three dimensions.

11
00:00:48,355 --> 00:00:51,349
Turn the garment around and look closer at the pattern.

12
00:00:51,469 --> 00:00:56,755
This is a concept preview, helping you imagine the look before making a physical piece.

13
00:01:00,350 --> 00:01:05,605
Here is a recorded try-on using a synthetic demo person and this matching source design.

14
00:01:05,725 --> 00:01:09,534
The image-editing service creates an approximate wearing preview.

15
00:01:09,654 --> 00:01:15,162
The original pattern stays visible for comparison, because AI can change details.

16
00:01:15,282 --> 00:01:19,910
It's a way to imagine wearing the design, rather than a promise of exact fit.

17
00:01:25,350 --> 00:01:28,844
Haziq directed the concept and prototype development.

18
00:01:28,964 --> 00:01:31,666
Timothy contributed ideation and testing.

19
00:01:31,786 --> 00:01:39,000
Codex helped us translate the idea into the guided workflow, shared pattern rendering, image integration and tests.

20
00:01:39,120 --> 00:01:44,060
We learned to separate exact design previews from AI appearance approximations.

21
00:01:45,350 --> 00:01:49,701
Next, we want artisan feedback and stronger real-device testing.

22
00:01:49,821 --> 00:01:54,346
Wear Your Batik: from appreciating a pattern to creating a look of your own.
